      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2506.23692v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        While AI for Science (AI4S) serves as an analytical tool in the current research paradigm, it doesn&#39;t solve its core inefficiency. We propose &#34;Agent for Science&#34; (Agent4S)-the use of LLM-driven agents to automate the entire research workflow-as the true Fifth Scientific Paradigm. This paper introduces a five-level classification for Agent4S, outlining a clear roadmap from simple task automation to&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2506.23692v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2506.23692v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
